{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall choose from all the people men of valor, etc.</b> Since the Sages said (Nedarim 38a) that the Holy One, blessed be He, rests His Presence only upon one who is mighty, wise, rich, and humble — and all of them were found in Moshe — therefore all four of these attributes are mentioned here, for a judge needs all of them. Thus it says 'and you shall choose' — through the holy spirit that is upon you, for from it shall be taken to bestow upon the elders who sit to judge, and they need to resemble you in all the attributes that are in you, for between the one who bestows and the one who receives there must be a likeness and a single correspondence, and all the virtues that are in you must also be in the judges. 'Men of valor' — these are the mighty of strength, whose strength then is as now, to break the high arms of those who say 'our hands are high,' for any judge who is weak of strength presumably transgresses 'you shall not withdraw from him.' 'Fearers of Elohim' — these are the humble, for humility leads to fear, as it says (Proverbs 22:4) 'עֵקֶב עֲנָוָה יִרְאַת ה׳.' Therefore it says 'יַדְרֵךְ עֲנָוִים בַּמִּשְׁפָּט' — for through humility one comes to fear, and all who are coarse of heart in halakhic ruling are foolish, wicked, and proud of spirit. 'Men of truth' — these are the wise, who know how to distinguish between truth and falsehood, in order to render a judgment of truth in truth, for what fool can be trained to distinguish between truth and falsehood? Without doubt he does not know and does not understand; in darkness he walks. 'Haters of unjust gain' — these are the rich, who have everything and took no unjust gain, for with any poor judge there is reason to suspect lest he take a bribe to pervert judgment." "And concerning these four classes, the psalmist said (Psalms 82:1) 'מִזְמוֹר לְאָסָף אֱלֹהִים נִצָּב בַּעֲדַת אֵל בְּקֶרֶב אֱלֹהִים יִשְׁפֹּט' — for the Holy One, blessed be He, stands to judge the judges of Israel for the injustice done among them; this is what it says, 'בְּקֶרֶב אֱלֹהִים' — that is, the judges whom He will judge, to speak justice with them. And He said, 'עַד מָתַי תִּשְׁפְּטוּ עָוֶל וּפְנֵי רְשָׁעִים תִּשְׂאוּ סֶלָה' (Psalms 82:2) — corresponding to the absence of fear, for when the judge does not fear Elohim and is proud of spirit, then he lifts the face of the wicked with great elevation, so that the wicked will honor him and exalt him too, on account of the haughtiness of the judge's heart that seeks self-aggrandizement. 'שִׁפְטוּ דַל וְיָתוֹם עָנִי וָרָשׁ הַצְדִּיקוּ' (Psalms 82:3) — this teaches that they were not rich and would take bribes; therefore no poor man or orphan who was righteous ever prevailed in his suit, for he had nothing to give the judge to bribe him. After that he said, 'פַּלְּטוּ דַל וְאֶבְיוֹן מִיַּד רְשָׁעִים הַצִּילוּ' (Psalms 82:4) — for they would appoint weak judges who had no power to rescue and save the poor man from the hand of one stronger than he. After that he said, 'לֹא יָדְעוּ וְלֹא יָבִינוּ בַּחֲשֵׁכָה יִתְהַלָּכוּ' (Psalms 82:5) — for they would appoint a judge who is not expert and not practiced, lacking wisdom; therefore they did not know right from left and did not understand truth from falsehood; therefore 'יִמּוֹטוּ כָּל מוֹסְדֵי אָרֶץ' (Psalms 82:5) — for on justice the world stands, and when the foundation is corrupted, the structure built upon it also falls. 'אֲנִי אָמַרְתִּי אֱלֹהִים אַתֶּם' (Psalms 82:6) — for one who judges a judgment of truth in truth is as though he is made a partner with the Holy One, blessed be He, to be as Elohim. 'אָכֵן כְּאָדָם תְּמוּתוּן' (Psalms 82:7) — for he too caused the corruption of the world like you. 'קוּמָה אֱלֹהִים שָׁפְטָה הָאָרֶץ' (Psalms 82:8) — for when there is no justice below there is justice above, for 'הַמִּשְׁפָּט לֵאלֹהִים הוּא' (Deuteronomy 1:17). And all that the judge takes from this one unjustly, the Holy One, blessed be He, restores and bequeaths it from His own — this is what it says, 'כִּי אַתָּה תִנְחַל בְּכָל הַגּוֹיִם' (Psalms 82:8). Upon You it devolves to bequeath to them; therefore 'הַמִּשְׁפָּט לֵאלֹהִים הוּא' (Deuteronomy 1:17)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:21:25.093257694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}